<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 4.6 Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Practice Makes Perfect</heading>
    <paragraph>Evaluate the Determinant of a 2 × 2 Matrix</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, evaluate the determinant of each square matrix.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="232" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack \begin{array}{l} {6-2} \\ {3-1} \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="233" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack \begin{array}{l} {-4 8} \\ {-3 5} \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>4</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="234" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack \begin{array}{rccr} -3 &amp; &amp; &amp; 5 \\ 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="235" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack \begin{array}{rccr} -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 \\ 7 &amp; &amp; &amp; -5 \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>10</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Evaluate the Determinant of a 3 × 3 Matrix</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, find and then evaluate the indicated minors.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="236" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{rccrccr} 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 4 \\ -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 \\ -4 &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 5 \end{array} \right|$$ Find the minor ⓐ $$a_{1}$$ ⓑ $$b_{2}$$ ⓒ $$c_{3}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="237" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{rccrccr} -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 \\ 4 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 \\ -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 \end{array} \right|$$ Find the minor ⓐ $$a_{1}$$ ⓑ $$b_{1}$$ ⓒ $$c_{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ 6 ⓑ $$-14-14$$ ⓒ $$-6-6$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="238" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{rccrccr} 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 \\ -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 \\ 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 \end{array} \right|$$ Find the minor ⓐ $$a_{2}$$ ⓑ $$b_{2}$$ ⓒ $$c_{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="239" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{rccrccr} -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 3 \\ 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 \\ -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 \end{array} \right|$$ Find the minor ⓐ $$a_{3}$$ ⓑ $$b_{3}$$ ⓒ $$c_{3}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ 9 ⓑ $$-3-3$$ ⓒ 8</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, evaluate each determinant by expanding by minors along the first row.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="240" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{rccrccr} -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 \\ -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 \\ 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 \end{array} \right|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="241" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{rccrccr} 4 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 \\ -3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 \\ -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -5 &amp; &amp; &amp; 7 \end{array} \right|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$-77 -77$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="242" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{rccrccr} -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 \\ 5 &amp; &amp; &amp; -6 &amp; &amp; &amp; 7 \\ -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 \end{array} \right|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="243" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{lccrccr} 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 \\ 5 &amp; &amp; &amp; -6 &amp; &amp; &amp; 4 \\ 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 \end{array} \right|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>49</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, evaluate each determinant by expanding by minors.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="244" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{rccrccr} -5 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 \\ 4 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 \\ 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 6 \end{array} \right|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="245" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{rccrccr} 4 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 3 \\ 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 \\ -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; 4 \end{array} \right|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$-24 -24$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="246" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{rccrccr} 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; 5 &amp; &amp; &amp; 4 \\ -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 \\ -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 6 &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 \end{array} \right|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="247" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left| \begin{array}{lccrccr} 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 \\ 5 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 \\ 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 \end{array} \right|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>25</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Use Cramer’s Rule to Solve Systems of Equations</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, solve each system of equations using Cramer’s Rule.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="248" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {-2x + 3y = 3} \\ {x + 3y = 12} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="249" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x - 2y = -5} \\ {2x - 3y = -4} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( 7 , 6 ) ( 7 , 6 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="250" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x - 3y = -9} \\ {2x + 5y = 4} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="251" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x + y = -4} \\ {3x - 2y = -6} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( -2 , 0 ) ( -2 , 0 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="252" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x - 2y = -5} \\ {2x - 3y = -4} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="253" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x - 3y = -9} \\ {2x + 5y = 4} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( -3 , 2 ) ( -3 , 2 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="254" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {5x - 3y = -1} \\ {2x - y = 2} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="255" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {3x + 8y = -3} \\ {2x + 5y = -3} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( -9 , 3 ) ( -9 , 3 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="256" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {6x - 5y + 2z = 3} \\ {2x + y - 4z = 5} \\ {3x - 3y + z = -1} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="257" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {4x - 3y + z = 7} \\ {2x - 5y - 4z = 3} \\ {3x - 2y - 2z = -7} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( -3 , -5 , 4 ) ( -3 , -5 , 4 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="258" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x - 5y + 3z = 8} \\ {3x - y + 4z = 7} \\ {x + 3y + 2z = -3} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="259" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {11x + 9y + 2z = -9} \\ {7x + 5y + 3z = -7} \\ {4x + 3y + z = -3} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( 2 , -3 , -2 ) ( 2 , -3 , -2 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="260" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x + 2z = 0} \\ {4y + 3z = -2} \\ {2x - 5y = 3} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="261" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x + 5y = 4} \\ {3y - z = 3} \\ {4x + 3z = -3} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( -3 , 2 , 3 ) ( -3 , 2 , 3 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="262" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2y + 3z = -1} \\ {5x + 3y = -6} \\ {7x + z = 1} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="263" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {3x - z = -3} \\ {5y + 2z = -6} \\ {4x + 3y = -8} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( -2 , 0 , -3 ) ( -2 , 0 , -3 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="264" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x + y = 3} \\ {6x + 3y = 9} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="265" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x - 4y = -1} \\ {-3x + 12y = 3} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>infinitely many solutions</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="266" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {-3x - y = 4} \\ {6x + 2y = -16} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="267" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {4x + 3y = 2} \\ {20x + 15y = 5} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>inconsistent</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="268" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x + y - 3z = -1} \\ {y - z = 0} \\ {-x + 2y = 1} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="269" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x + 3y + z = 12} \\ {x + y + z = 9} \\ {3x + 4y + 2z = 20} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>inconsistent</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="270" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {3x + 4y - 3z = -2} \\ {2x + 3y - z = -12} \\ {x + y - 2z = 6} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="271" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{r} {x - 2y + 3z = 1} \\ {x + y - 3z = 7} \\ {3x - 4y + 5z = 7} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>infinitely many solutions</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Solve Applications Using Determinants</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, determine whether the given points are collinear.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="272" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {0,1} \right),$$ $$\left( {2,0} \right),$$ and $$\left( {-2,2} \right).$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="273" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {0,-5} \right),$$ $$\left( {-2,-2} \right),$$ and $$\left( {2,-8} \right).$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>yes</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="274" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {4,-3} \right),$$ $$\left( {6,-4} \right),$$ and $$\left( {2,-2} \right).$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="275" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {-2,1} \right),$$ $$\left( {-4,4} \right),$$ and $$\left( {0,-2} \right).$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>yes</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <heading level="1">Writing Exercises</heading>
    <exercise number="276" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Explain the difference between a square matrix and its determinant. Give an example of each.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="277" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Explain what is meant by the minor of an entry in a square matrix.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Answers will vary.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="278" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Explain how to decide which row or column you will use to expand a $$3 \times 3$$ determinant.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="279" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Explain the steps for solving a system of equations using Cramer’s rule.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Answers will vary.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
